From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:59:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] regulator: qcom_smd: ignore a disabled voter's voltage in
 the paired sleep set

The paired sleep-set request takes the maximum of the both-set vote, the
sleep-only vote and the boot hold. A disabled both-set voter keeps its
cached voltage for its next enable, so the remoteproc proxy MX requests
(1.2875 V, released after handover) still raised the sleep-only MX
request that CPR keeps enabled, and MX never reached retention. Count
the both-set voltage only while that voter is enabled.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
---
 drivers/regulator/qcom_smd-regulator.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/qcom_smd-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/qcom_smd-regulator.c
index fcfee8e96..4b55488e4 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom_smd-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom_smd-regulator.c
@@ -99,6 +99,13 @@ static struct rpm_reg_vote rpm_reg_pair_sleep_vote(struct rpm_reg_pair *pair,
 	const struct rpm_reg_vote *sleep_only = &pair->votes[2];
 	u64 load = (u64)vote.load + sleep_only->load;
 
+	/*
+	 * A disabled both-set voter keeps its cached voltage for its next
+	 * enable, but the RPM ignores the voltage of a disabled request. It must
+	 * not raise the request that the sleep-only voter keeps enabled.
+	 */
+	if (!vote.enabled)
+		vote.uV = 0;
 	if (pair->sleep_enable_valid)
 		vote.enabled = pair->sleep_enabled;
 	if (pair->sleep_voltage_valid)
